//? Title: Velocity Verlet: actual drift/kick operands and energy
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Newtonian position/velocity trajectories need time integration that respects
conservative dynamics over many steps. Velocity Verlet combines a position drift
with an average-acceleration velocity kick.
)

\toc

> The method

Use x_next=x+h*v+h²*a(x)/2 and v_next=v+h*(a(x)+a(x_next))/2. Taylor expansion
gives local O(h³) error and global second order for smooth acceleration. For the
unit harmonic oscillator and |h|<2, the update preserves the modified quadratic
v²+(1−h²/4)x². The physical energy(v²+x²)/2 oscillates within a step-dependent
band; it is not exactly conserved. Symplecticity requires the appropriate
conservative position-only force, not every arbitrary callback.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/verlet_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::velocity_verlet_work([](const std::vector<double> & x) {
        return std::vector<double>{-x[0]};
    }, {1}, {0}, 0, .1, 1, 1);
    auto q = r.steps[0];
    std::print("| old x | old v | old a | new a | actual x | actual v | calls " "|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---:|\n|`{}`|`{}`|`{}`|`{}`|`{}`|`{}`|{}|\n",
               q.before_x, q.before_v, q.old_acceleration, q.new_acceleration,
               q.after_x, q.after_v, r.acceleration_calls);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Oscillator x1,v0,h.1");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual drift x{}", q.after_x));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual kick v{}", q.after_v));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/verlet_tiny.svg");
}
```
