> Interpretation and limits

Initial state, callback shape/results and arithmetic are checked before indexed
use. Zero interval copies state without callback calls; backward integration is
supported. A nonzero interval whose represented step underflows to zero throws.
Output and capture budgets count scalar values. Arbitrary callback exceptions
propagate.

The complete editable C++ programs save figures locally; results contain
ordinary computed Markdown. Selected counters describe actual producer
operations, excluding validation when stated.

